        ['Explain the stored program concept and one limitation of the von Neumann architecture.', ['Instructions and data share memory', 'Fetched as needed', 'Bottleneck explained'], 'In the stored program concept, program instructions and data are stored together in the same main memory and fetched by the CPU as needed. A limitation is the von Neumann bottleneck: because instructions and data share one bus, the CPU often waits for memory transfers.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 3, 'theory', 5],
